From: Codex local A376B compatibility adaptation
Subject: [PATCH] Retain AZH4 donor KnoxPatch and attestation behavior

Reason: attempt36.txt:1259-1260, 1265-1260, 1297-1310, 1343-1348 and
1360-1388 show KnoxPatch relies on stale integrity-attestation call sites across
DevicePolicyManagerService, DarManagerService, UserManagerService,
AttestParameterSpec, AttestationUtils and SemSsdidManagerService. Skip this
optional module as a whole for the exact AZH4 M2 donor to avoid partial security
behavior changes and preserve AZH4's Knox/attestation implementation.
Files: scripts/internal/apply_modules.sh.
Verification: exact module/profile guard, bash -n, replay68 and clean attempt37.
This M2 build omits the fork's KnoxPatch spoof/bypass features; revert0068 to port.

---
